cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "anny-soma-corpus: ANNY-SOMA keypoint corpus for RFD 1173"
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, please cite it and the upstream sources
  listed under `references`.
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    alias: fire
    website: https://github.com/fire
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: https://apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
type: dataset
version: RFD-2203
date-released: "2026-09-04"
url: https://huggingface.co/datasets/chibifire/anny-soma-corpus
repository-code: https://github.com/weftspun/anny-soma-corpus
identifiers:
  - type: other
    value: urn:oid:1.3.6.1.4.1.66606.1.2.2203
    description: RFD 2203 (first-subset row shape for the ANNY-SOMA keypoint corpus)
  - type: other
    value: urn:oid:1.3.6.1.4.1.66606.1.2.1173
    description: RFD 1173 (a multimodal diffusion pipeline; parent RFD)
  - type: other
    value: urn:oid:1.3.6.1.4.1.66606.1.2.2196
    description: RFD 2196 (HuggingFace dataset viewer rules)
keywords:
  - keypoints
  - motion
  - anny
  - soma
  - kimodo
  - rfd-1173
  - rfd-2203
references:
  # ANNY -- Apache-2.0 (courtesy citation; the mesh, rig, and blendshape targets this corpus poses)
  - type: software
    title: "anny"
    authors:
      - name: "NAVER Corp."
    repository-code: https://github.com/naver/anny
    license: Apache-2.0
    notes: >-
      Mesh (makehuman 19,158-vertex topology via TopologyConfig
      base_mesh="makehuman", remove_unattached_vertices=False), SOMA
      rig, and the 52 facial-action blendshape targets under
      data/faceunits01/targets/faceunits/. wholebody133.pth is
      indexed against this mesh.
  # Kimodo -- Apache-2.0 code + NVIDIA Open Model License weights (courtesy citation; the motion source)
  - type: software
    title: "kimodo"
    authors:
      - name: "NVIDIA"
    repository-code: https://github.com/nv-tlabs/kimodo
    license: Apache-2.0
    notes: >-
      Kimodo-SOMA-* checkpoints under NVIDIA Open Model License.
      Kimodo emits (T, 77, 3, 3) local rotation matrices which are
      converted to axis-angle rotvecs; anny prepends one root identity
      at call time to reach 78 pose parameters (task #76 for the
      disambiguation of 77-vs-78 across RFDs 1102/1173/2162).
  # Pixal3D -- Apache-2.0 (courtesy citation; the view-schedule origin)
  - type: software
    title: "pixal3d"
    repository-code: https://github.com/weftspun/pixal3d-upstream
    license: Apache-2.0
    notes: >-
      Vetted Z-up port of the sphere_hammersley_sequence camera
      schedule at pixal3d/utils/random_utils.py:22, imported via
      6-datasource/anny-render-corpus. Camera policy per CLAUDE.md
      convention "Views come from the sphere_hammersley_sequence
      camera sequence".
  # wholebody133 anchors -- Apache-2.0 (courtesy citation; the anchor source, part-derived from NAVER's coco.pth)
  - type: software
    title: "anny-keypoint-anchors"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    repository-code: https://github.com/weftspun/anny-keypoint-anchors
    license: Apache-2.0 OR MIT
    notes: >-
      The 133 COCO-WholeBody keypoint anchors as vertex weights over
      ANNY's 19,158-vertex makehuman mesh. Body 17 + feet 6 imported
      from NAVER's coco.pth verbatim; hands 42 built from ANNY's own
      skinning weights; face 68 (v3) built from per-target top-decile
      motion filter over the 52 facial-action blendshapes, filtered
      against SOMA_wrap's excluded-vertex set. Each subset's manifest
      records which SHA of wholebody133.pth it was baked against.
  # RFD 2203 -- the row shape decision
  - type: generic
    title: "RFD 2203: The first-subset row shape for the anny-soma keypoint corpus"
    url: https://github.com/weftspun/request-for-discussion/tree/main/rfd/2203-anny-soma-first-subset-corpus-shape
    notes: Row shape and publish path are decided here.
  # RFD 1173 -- the parent pipeline this feeds
  - type: generic
    title: "RFD 1173: A multimodal diffusion pipeline"
    url: https://github.com/weftspun/request-for-discussion/tree/main/rfd/1173-a-multimodal-diffusion-pipeline
    notes: This corpus feeds the RFD 1173 keypoints stub.
  # NASA RP-1024 -- public-domain anatomical ROM source for the anny-tpose-sweep joint envelope
  - type: report
    title: "Anthropometric Source Book, Volume I: Anthropometry for Designers"
    authors:
      - name: "NASA (Anthropology Research Project)"
    number: NASA-RP-1024-VOL-1
    year: 1978
    url: https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/19790003563
    license: "public-domain-us-federal"
    notes: >-
      Work of the US Government per 17 USC 105; NTRS record declares "Work
      of the US Gov. Public Use Permitted", Distribution: Public. Chapter VI
      Tables 1 and 2 supply the anatomical joint ROM envelope used to bound
      the `anny-tpose-sweep` motion source's parametric sweep ranges (see
      `sources/anatomy-rom-envelope.json`). Table 1 reproduces data from
      Barter, Emanuel and Truett 1957 (a WADC Technical Report — Wright
      Air Development Center, US Air Force, also PD by 17 USC 105).
      Table 2 reproduces data from Harris and Harris 1968; provenance not
      independently verified this pass, noted per CLAUDE.md rule 3.
  # RFD 2196 -- the HF publishing rules
  - type: generic
    title: "RFD 2196: HuggingFace dataset viewer rules"
    url: https://github.com/weftspun/request-for-discussion/tree/main/rfd/2196-huggingface-dataset-viewer-rules
    notes: Publish path (LFS + hf_transfer, xet disabled, hf upload-large-folder) per rule 5.
